    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Five-week review, four weeks on omeprazole: reflux, biopsy result, sleep, and the remedy. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Aurelius returns four weeks after his endoscopy. The burning after meals eased within a week of starting omeprazole and has now gone, and he no longer wakes with a sour taste. He takes the capsule before breakfast each day, eats his main meal early in the evening and has raised the head of his bed. His appetite has come back and he has gained weight. He has had two CBT-I sessions, the first a fortnight ago, and keeps a sleep diary: he now goes to bed only when sleepy and gets up at a fixed hour. Ten days ago he decided, on his own, to take the herbal paste only on alternate nights. For the first three or four nights without it he felt restless and slept badly; that has settled, and he has no craving for it. He has not increased the amount on the nights he takes it. His stools are regular with polyethylene glycol two or three times a week. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Reflux</td><td>Gone on omeprazole; no night waking from it</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Two CBT-I sessions; Insomnia Severity Index 12</td></tr><tr><td>Remedy</td><td>Alternate nights for ten days, by his choice; brief restlessness that settled; no craving</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Constitutional</td><td>Negative</td><td>Appetite better; weight up; less tired</td></tr><tr><td>Gastrointestinal</td><td>Negative</td><td>No heartburn, pain after meals, difficulty swallowing, vomiting or black stools</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Negative</td><td>No chest pain</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Positive</td><td>Sleep improving but still short; mood better; no thoughts of self-harm</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>4 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

